Package: PlaceboLM
Title: Causal Progress with Imperfect Placebos Using Linear Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam", "Rohde", , "adamrohde@ucla.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-1825-1234"))
Description: Implements the partial-identification framework of Rohde and
    Hazlett (2025) for making causal progress with imperfect placebo variables.
    Given a placebo outcome or placebo treatment that shares confounders with
    the treatment-outcome relationship of interest, the package allows users to
    specify ranges of sensitivity parameters (a confounding ratio k and a
    residual placebo association) and produces estimates, bootstrap confidence
    intervals, summary tables, contour plots, and line plots over the
    parameter space. Special cases include selection-on-observables (k = 0)
    and the difference-in-differences benchmark. See Rohde and Hazlett (2025)
    <doi:10.1093/jrsssa/qnaf001>.
